### Task B2: Core Domain Classes Justification
1. Student Represents the primary user who requests and holds equipment reservations within the system
2. Booking: Represents the central domain concept containing reservation dates, status, and item associations
3. Equipment: Represents the physical resource being reserved and managed for availability
4. Staff Member: Represents the administrative role responsible for reviewing booking requests and overseeing equipment

### Task B3: Identification of Uncertainty
Candidate Attribute:emailAddres for Student or status for Booking
Uncertainty:While recording an email or booking status is logically useful, FR01–FR06 do not explicitly specify how notifications or approval states are stored
Target Stakeholder: College Facilities Manager / System Administrator



## Part D & E — Associations, Multiplicities & Open Questions

### Relationships Summary
Student makes Booking
Booking identifies Equipment
Staff Member reviews Booking
Staff Member manages availability of Equipment

### Confirmed Multiplicity
FR02: Each booking identifies exactly one equipment item
Multiplicity of 1 is applied at the Equipment end of the Booking–Equipment association

### Open Questions (Uncertainty Analysis)
1. Student — Booking: Can a booking be made jointly on behalf of multiple students, or is it strictly tied to exactly one student
2. Booking — Equipment: How many historical or future bookings can reference the same equipment item over time (`0..*`)
3. Staff Member — Booking: Is each booking reviewed by exactly one assigned staff member, or can multiple staff members review the same request
4. Staff Member — Equipment: Can multiple staff members manage the same equipment item, or is equipment divided among specific staff



